 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Contacts and plug",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The mating plug is Ø3.5 mm with a 14 mm shaft; from the body outward its rings are sleeve (pin 1), ring (pin 3) and tip (pin 2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Tip switch",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "On SJ-3524 pin 4 touches the tip spring while the socket is empty, so pins 2 and 4 are joined; inserting a plug breaks that contact. SJ-3523 has no pin 4."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The jack sits on flat solder tabs (terminals 1 to 3, plus terminal 4 on SJ-3524) and two Ø1.5 mm posts that go into Ø1.70 holes in the board. The nose projects 2.5 mm in front of the 14.5 mm body outline, and terminal 4 comes out of the rear end. General tolerances: X ±0.5 mm, X.X ±0.3 mm, X.XX ±0.20 mm, board pattern ±0.05 mm."
  }
 ],
